Gear augmentation is a set of crafts for making gear into other gear.  It
exists so that a fine piece you cannot use is worth something anyway: the
wrong size, the wrong class, the wrong slot.  Nothing in it is faster than
hunting.  It is the slow road, and it costs more than it returns.

THE TWO LINES

Metal and cloth work the same way on opposite sides.

  SMELT  turns any metal thing into an ingot     WEAVE  turns any soft thing
  FORGE  turns an ingot into armor or a weapon          into a skein
         FORGE RESIZE  fits a piece to a body    SEW    turns a skein into
         FORGE REFIT   moves it to a new slot           clothing or light
         FORGE COMBINE makes a bigger bar               SEW REFIT moves a
                                                        piece to a new slot
                                                 TAILOR fits a piece to a body

Both break-down skills grade what they produce from how cleanly the work
went, and both build-up skills spend that grade: a poor bar makes a poorer
piece and loses more of what it carried.

THE LADDER

  STRIP    cuts a piece down a tier, widening who can wear it
  PLATE    builds a piece up a tier, narrowing it, capped by hardness
  BANGLE   drops anything to jewelry, half the armor for twice the stats
  BOLSTER  raises a piece's armor toward the most its tier allows

TRANSMUTE changes what a thing is made of, which is what lets a soft piece
climb the ladder at all, and the only way between the two lines.

THE SOUL OF A THING

Stats survive everything.  They ride in ingots, in skeins, in the offcuts a
resize leaves behind, and they come out the far end of the work.

  DISTILL  destroys jewelry and yields its stats as essence
  INFUSE   spends an essence to write a stat onto a piece
  RITES    draws a soul from a corpse into a soulstone
  ENSOUL   makes a soulstone out of an opal

RAW MATERIAL

  MINE     cuts ore out of hills, mountains and caves

